From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:16:43 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] pcecd-carts

A PC Engine CD game is drawn as a CD jewel case, the same object the
PlayStation shelf draws (ADR 0069): one 142 x 125 mm three-piece case, the
front cover from Labels/PCECD/<stem>.png in the square well, and on insert
the case opens and the disc, printed from Labels/PCECD/disc/<stem>.png,
goes into the slot. A disc tagged (Japan) wears the paper spine strip
(obi) that Japanese discs, games included, carry over the left side of the
case; every other disc wears the plain case. The region comes from the
file name tags only: a PC Engine disc has no SYSTEM.CNF serial, and no
playlist turns one into a double case. The disc art path falls back to
the cart's own shelf folder instead of the PlayStation one.
